    "status": "DRAFT. Neither held staging has been prototyped or shown to a tester, and clean_gate has not been either. Nothing here is proven. The Technical Designer builds the prototype below; the tester question 'Results felt fair and believable' decides between the held stagings.",
    "prototype": {
      "status": "NOT BUILT. Every line below is a brief, not a result.",
      "build": [
        "One throwaway Godot scene with no simulation link that plays 60.0 s to 75.0 s from this file, for three endings: clean_gate (W wins fight_late), held_island and held_gate (W loses it). Both held endings use the same fixture: W leads, U wins the last fight, the lead number steps down and stays positive (ACTION-VOCABULARY HF3).",
        "Tokens at 36 px (ART-BIBLE 3.8: a teal circle for the player's side, a coral hexagon for the other), the reserve pack as six 14 px dots at rush speed, guard towers falling at tower_tally.guard_fall_s, Cairn crack and fall from the variant's events. Every position, leg and event time is read from this file; none is typed into the scene.",
        "Both seats: the player as W and the player as U, flipped as in the view block.",
        "Print for each run: each leg's arrival time against arrive_by_s, the smallest gap between two tokens in the formation, and the frame time (budget: 10 tokens, 6 dots, 4 guard towers)."],
      "measure": [
        "Tester question 1, after each ending: 'The result felt fair and believable', 1 to 5.",
        "Tester question 2: 'Who won the last fight?' (you, them, not sure).",
        "Tester question 3: 'Why did the Cairn fall?' (the lead was bigger, the last fight, not sure)."],
      "decision_rule": "Proposal, not a ruling. At least 5 testers who have not seen the plan; each sees clean_gate first (the control), then held_island and held_gate in random order. A staging passes if its mean on question 1 is at least 4.0 (the Alpha 0.7 acceptance bar), at least 4 of 5 name U as the last fight's winner, and at least 3 of 5 answer 'the lead was bigger'. If both pass, ship held_island (no hero walks) unless held_gate's mean is higher by 0.5 or more. If one passes, ship that one. If neither passes, the staging is not shipped as drawn; do not fix it by letting W win the last fight on screen (that breaks HF1 and invariant I9); send it back to the Gameplay and Systems Designers. What this cannot tell: touch feel, speed or heat on a phone, or whether five testers are enough (they are a screen, not a proof)."
    },
